+/**
+ * Process-wide singleton "owner" wrapper around pimServiceLoop, the install
+ * step that installs/removes/starts/stops Windows services. One of 7
+ * near-identical Loop-owner wrapper singletons in pim_core. Also owns the
+ * class-static serviceAction field that tells pimServiceLoop::OnExecute()
+ * which of Install/Start/Stop to perform (set via setServiceAction()
+ * immediately before every Create() call at the confirmed call site).
+ *
+ * CONFIRMED HIGH-SEVERITY FINDING: unlike every one of its 6 sibling
+ * wrappers, Create_low() releases its xmlMutex lock IMMEDIATELY after
+ * starting the operation's thread, not after the operation completes (the
+ * trailing "will be released ... when done" comment is a stale copy-paste
+ * from the sibling classes and is factually wrong here). Consequence: a
+ * second Create()/Uninstall() call made while a prior pimServiceLoop is
+ * still running will succeed at TryLock() (since it is already unlocked),
+ * then delete the still-running pimServiceLoop out from under its own
+ * thread -- a genuine use-after-free / destroy-while-running race. This is
+ * currently latent because no traced caller in this codebase invokes this
+ * class concurrently, but it is live, reachable code, not gated behind any
+ * dead-code marker. Do not add a concurrent caller of this class without
+ * first relocating the xmlMutex.Unlock() call to Status()'s done-branch and
+ * Kill(), matching the other 6 wrappers' pattern.
+ *
+ * Also confirmed gap (shared with pimShortcuts/pimRegEdit/pimDownloader):
+ * Cancel() only sets a flag; the owned pimServiceLoop is not stopped by it.
+ *
+ * Sole caller in this codebase: pimEntitlement.
+ */
 class pimServices
 {
 private:
